				<div class="et_pb_text_inner"><h6><strong>Anne Hendrickx</strong></h6></div>
			</div><div class="et_pb_module et_pb_text et_pb_text_15_tb_body  et_pb_text_align_left et_pb_bg_layout_light">
				
				
				
				
				<div class="et_pb_text_inner"><p>Anne Hendrickx holds a Master in Economics from the Université Libre de Bruxelles. After nine years in humanitarian non-governmental organisations, she became an advisor on drug policy in the cabinet of the Minister of Social Affairs and Public Health in 2003. Since 2015, she has been an advisor in the Research Department of the Belgian Mutual Fund Solidaris, focusing on national and european issues relating to medicines. She is a member of the Committee for Reimbursement of Medicines of the Belgian National Institute for Health and Disability Insurance and of AIM’s Working Group on pharmaceuticals and medical devices, where she leads the “European model for fair prices of medicines” project.</p></div>
