				<div class="et_pb_text_inner"><h6><strong>Benjamin P. Geisler</strong></h6></div>
			</div><div class="et_pb_module et_pb_text et_pb_text_17_tb_body  et_pb_text_align_left et_pb_bg_layout_light">
				
				
				
				
				<div class="et_pb_text_inner"><p>Benjamin P. Geisler is a German-American board-certified internist who earned his medical degree at Charité – Universitätsmedizin Berlin. After a decision-sciences research fellowship in Boston, Ben completed an MPH at Harvard and an internal medicine residency at NYU School of Medicine. He then worked as an attending at Massachusetts General Hospital, instructor at Harvard Medical School, and senior consultant in early HTA for medical device companies. Passionate about clinically relevant outcomes research, Ben has also worked in research groups in Adelaide, Australia and Munich, Germany. In 2022, he relocated to Oslo, Norway where he is currently a doctoral research fellow in health economics.</p></div>
