				<div class="et_pb_text_inner"><h6><strong>Charlotte Roffiaen</strong></h6></div>
			</div><div class="et_pb_module et_pb_text et_pb_text_19_tb_body  et_pb_text_align_left et_pb_bg_layout_light">
				
				
				
				
				<div class="et_pb_text_inner"><p>Charlotte Roffiaen is a Sciences Po Paris graduate and trained lawyer specialised in EU law. She has been involved in health advocacy since 2001 and has advised France Assos Santé on its European strategy since 2010, focusing on access to medicines. France Assos Santé represents around 100 healthcare users’ organisations and is an active member of the European Patients’ Forum (EPF). Charlotte has also represented patients and consumers at the European Medicines Agency within the Executive Steering Group on Shortages and Safety of Medicinal Products (MSSG). Previously, she managed two European organisations: Active Citizenship Network and Lymphoma Coalition Europe.</p></div>
