				<div class="et_pb_text_inner"><h6>Dominik Griebling</h6></div>
			</div><div class="et_pb_module et_pb_text et_pb_text_21_tb_body  et_pb_text_align_left et_pb_bg_layout_light">
				
				
				
				
				<div class="et_pb_text_inner"><p><span>Dominik Griebling is Senior Manager Scientific Strategy &amp; Project Coordination at Fresenius SE &amp; Co. KGaA, Germany. He holds an MSc in Biomedicine from the University of Würzburg and has worked across Fresenius at the interface of science, strategy and business for nearly seven years. He coordinates the IHI-funded EU project EASYGEN, developing an automated platform for decentralised, point-of-care manufacturing of CAR T-cell therapies, and co-leads its work on next-generation CAR-T gene editing technologies. He contributes the EASYGEN perspective on improving access to CAR T-cell therapies and is co-first author of a 2026 </span><em><span>Cytotherapy</span></em><span> perspective addressing access barriers.</span></p></div>
