				<div class="et_pb_module et_pb_text et_pb_text_24_tb_body  et_pb_text_align_left et_pb_bg_layout_light">
				
				
				
				
				<div class="et_pb_text_inner"><h6>Elizabeth Macintyre</h6></div>
			</div><div class="et_pb_module et_pb_text et_pb_text_25_tb_body  et_pb_text_align_left et_pb_bg_layout_light">
				
				
				
				
				<div class="et_pb_text_inner"><p>Elizabeth Macintyre is Franco-Scottish and trained in Internal Medicine/Hematology in England, completed her PhD in Paris and her Post-Doctoral studies at Harvard. Professor of Hematology at Université Paris Cité since 1992, she headed Diagnostic Hematology at Necker–Enfants Malades Hospital from 1999–2018 and co-directs an INSERM team on lymphoid malignancies. She was President of the European Hematology Association from 2021–23 and of the Biomedical Alliance in Europe from 2024–25. She is currently a stakeholder in the European Commission Medical Devices Coordination Group and has recently joined the European School of Hematology executive board.</p></div>
