				<div class="et_pb_text_inner"><h6><strong>Frank-Ulrich Fricke</strong></h6></div>
			</div><div class="et_pb_module et_pb_text et_pb_text_27_tb_body  et_pb_text_align_left et_pb_bg_layout_light">
				
				
				
				
				<div class="et_pb_text_inner"><p>Prof. Dr. Frank-Ulrich Fricke is Professor of Health Economics at Technische Hochschule Nürnberg Georg Simon Ohm. He studied business administration at the Universities of Bayreuth and Kiel and worked as a research associate in economics, with a focus on health economics, at the University of Bayreuth. His professional experience includes positions at Medical Relations, Novartis Pharma Germany, Fricke &amp; Pirk, and IMS Health Economics &amp; Outcomes Research. From 2011 to 2015, he served as Deputy Member of the German Arbitration Board on Drug Prices and has been a full member since July 2015. He served as Faculty Dean from 2017 to 2026.</p></div>
