				<div class="et_pb_text_inner"><h6><strong>Frederick Thielen</strong></h6></div>
			</div><div class="et_pb_module et_pb_text et_pb_text_29_tb_body  et_pb_text_align_left et_pb_bg_layout_light">
				
				
				
				
				<div class="et_pb_text_inner"><p>Frederick Thielen is Assistant Professor at the Erasmus School of Health Policy and Management, Erasmus University Rotterdam, and Senior Scientific Researcher at the Trimbos Institute in Utrecht. His research focuses on health economics and outcomes studies. He has extensive experience in international project collaborations and is involved in several research consortia, including European Horizon projects. A nurse by background, he worked at the internal medicine ward of University Hospital Aachen. He studied European Public Health and Health Sciences at Maastricht University and obtained his PhD from Erasmus University Rotterdam in 2020, focusing on challenges in health technology assessment and haemato-oncology.</p></div>
