				<div class="et_pb_text_inner"><h6>Pia Henkel</h6></div>
			</div><div class="et_pb_module et_pb_text et_pb_text_41_tb_body  et_pb_text_align_left et_pb_bg_layout_light">
				
				
				
				
				<div class="et_pb_text_inner"><p>Pia Sofie Henkel is a Doctoral Research Fellow at the Department of Health Management and Health Economics at the University of Oslo. Her research focuses on health economic evaluation and modelling, next-generation sequencing for precision cancer medicine, and integrating environmental aspects into economic assessments. She is also interested in European HTA processes and improving market access to innovative health technologies. Pia holds a European Master in Health Economics and Management (EU-HEM, 2022) and a Bachelor of Arts in International Business (2018) from accadis Hochschule Bad Homburg, Germany, providing a strong foundation for her research in health economics.</p></div>
