				<div class="et_pb_text_inner"><h6><strong>Robin Doeswijk</strong></h6></div>
			</div><div class="et_pb_module et_pb_text et_pb_text_43_tb_body  et_pb_text_align_left et_pb_bg_layout_light">
				
				
				
				
				<div class="et_pb_text_inner"><p>Robin Doeswijk is Head of European Affairs at the European Hematology Association (EHA), representing hematology professionals across Europe and beyond. With a background in International Relations and public affairs, he oversees EHA’s policy, advocacy and regulatory work, partnerships and alliances. EHA’s policy and regulatory work focuses on improving affordable and equal access to innovative therapies, with particular attention to EU Health Technology Assessment and the cost-benefit assessment and pricing of new medicines. He chairs the BioMed Alliance HTA Working Group and is a member of the EMA HCP Working Party, as well as a faculty member of the European Access Academy.</p></div>
