				<div class="et_pb_text_inner"><h6>Stavros Anagnostopoulos</h6></div>
			</div><div class="et_pb_module et_pb_text et_pb_text_49_tb_body  et_pb_text_align_left et_pb_bg_layout_light">
				
				
				
				
				<div class="et_pb_text_inner"><p>Stavros Anagnostopoulos, MSc, is a researcher at the Institute for Medical Technology Assessment (iMTA). He holds a Pharmacy degree from the Aristotle University of Thessaloniki (2021), and a master&#8217;s degree in Health Economics, Policy &amp; Law from Erasmus University Rotterdam (2022), with his master&#8217;s thesis assessing the effects informal care on carers&#8217; mental health in the Dutch setting. Since joining iMTA in 2023, Stavros has been involved in various health economics research projects, with a focus on health technology assessments, including cost-effectiveness modelling and systematic reviews across a range of disease areas and Treatments.</p></div>
