				<div class="et_pb_text_inner"><h6>Steven Hartjes</h6></div>
			</div><div class="et_pb_module et_pb_text et_pb_text_51_tb_body  et_pb_text_align_left et_pb_bg_layout_light">
				
				
				
				
				<div class="et_pb_text_inner"><p>Steven Hartjes is a patient advocate at Hematon, the Dutch patient organisation for leukemia, lymphoma and myeloma. A former patient, he joined Hematon in 2021. He has a background in business economics and spent his 40-year career at EY Auditors, including extensive work in data analytics. He is currently an unpaid guest researcher at Leiden University Medical Center, focusing on generating Real World Evidence using healthcare insurance data. He represents Hematon in the global Lymphoma Coalition, serves on the Steering Committee of RWD4decisions as a patient advocate, and is a member of the Lymphoma Coalition’s HTA special interest group.</p></div>
