				<div class="et_pb_text_inner"><h6><strong>Zoltán Kaló </strong></h6></div>
			</div><div class="et_pb_module et_pb_text et_pb_text_55_tb_body  et_pb_text_align_left et_pb_bg_layout_light">
				
				
				
				
				<div class="et_pb_text_inner"><p>Prof. Zoltán Kaló is Director General of the Hungarian National Health Insurance Fund and Professor of Health Economics at the Center for Health Technology Assessment at Semmelweis University in Budapest. For 18 years, he was the lead partner of Syreon Research Institute. He has over 30 years of international experience in academia and industry, specialising in health systems design, healthcare financing, health technology assessment, patient access and pricing policies. During his career, Dr. Kaló has served as a policy advisor to public decision-makers, global healthcare corporations and scientific societies. In 2021, he received the ISPOR Marilyn Dix Smith Leadership Award.</p></div>
